      "description": "Separate auth system entirely: organizer_members on the auth:organizer guard, logging in with uid + password, scoped to one event. These are the staff an EO hires - gate officers scanning tickets, ticket agents selling walk-ins - not the EO themselves. Uses {{organizer_token}}, not {{platform_token}}."
    },
    {
      "name": "Super Admin Console",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Admin Summary",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/admin/summary",
            "description": "Dashboard counters. Returns a flat object, not a list:\n\npending_events, verified_events, active_users, active_categories,\npending_talents, refunds_requiring_attention, webhooks_requiring_attention\n\nThe last two are operational alerts - non-zero means someone should look at the two queues below."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refund Queue",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/admin/operations/refunds?limit=20",
            "description": "Payments with requires_refund = true: real money owed back. Set when a buyer paid twice (they switched payment method and paid both) or paid an order the expiry sweeper had already released.\n\nPaginated (meta.page/limit/pages), newest paid first, limit capped at 100.\nRows: id, reference_id, order_number, provider, status, amount, paid_at.\n\nNothing clears this automatically - it is a work queue, not a log."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Webhook Attention Queue",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/admin/operations/webhooks?limit=20",
            "description": "Webhook deliveries with status 'unmatched' or 'failed'.\n\n  unmatched - verified callback that matched no payment; money may have moved\n              with nothing on our side to attach it to\n  failed    - processing threw; error column holds why, and the provider retries\n\nPaginated, newest first, limit capped at 100.\nRows: id, provider, event_type, reference_id, status, error, created_at."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List Admin Categories",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{base_url}}/admin/categories?limit=20"
          }
        },
